    "summary": "Fresh Astra single-pass visual reading of all 24 prepared pages: five Bulgarian manuscript pages, all four solution images, both criterion sheets, all nine English question/reference PDF pages and all four standalone reference images. Earlier English Astra transcriptions reused after source comparison. All nine Bulgarian original whole-problem IDs retained. Native official sketches, grading criteria and reference tables restored. No separate model checker.",
    "sourceGaps": [
      "The transit key prints “December 31, 2017” in an intermediate line, while its calculations and final answer concern 2117.",
      "The orbital-radius formula retains the source’s linear slash and multiplication notation; the Moon-comparison formula likewise retains the printed placement of T_M and omega_P. The key explicitly permits a bonus for noting that the resulting orbit is outside Earth’s Hill sphere.",
      "The Mars key calculates about 2130 km but prints ~2300 km in its final answer. The requested Bear-and-Penguin drawing earns one point, but no completed drawing is supplied in the official key.",
      "The galaxy key prints 3.74+7.5=10.24 and M=−28.2, followed by a −0.2 correction and approximately 20 trillion stars; these printed inconsistent values are retained. Its listed criteria total 9 points (3+3+1+2), unlike the general note about 8 points, so the problem total remains unspecified.",
      "The native planetary table follows the English PDF reference page (Mercury inclination 7.00°). The separately archived data_1.png instead prints 7.01°. Both source files were read; the discrepancy is retained here.",
      "The Bulgarian manuscript’s nine IDs and shared αβ / distinct α and β tasks are retained. Full English sketches, both criterion sheets, all four standalone reference images and both English question editions were read. No Bulgarian official key is present in the full year inventory. The supplied sketches explicitly are not complete pedagogical solutions; no missing derivations are invented."
    ],
